lthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging, so we did not use it.) After the rollback, the service is healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 14974, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017yeYqkFr9UHdg2yiGBETXo", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 14974, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017yeYqkFr9UHdg2yiGBETXo", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18048, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident for it, INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc is newer, but it was only ever healthy in staging, so it didn't qualify.\n- **Rollback:** us-east, us-west and eu-west all moved from v2.3.1 to v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** It says what happened, why I picked v2.3.0, and the results after the rollback. It also says the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure still needs to be found before v2.3.1 is redeployed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PRyE7sZvn9z6n5VQBMV7PC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01H8Keip2JC3Wc35k7aLA9T8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0 (v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging, so it doesn't qualify).", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FVtRs6e5LJ1xSoXhKpDVWN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PPmQJaE9qGTgVrcyf2HFvZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WrKm9dNBcNGALekFydEAkW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017yeYqkFr9UHdg2yiGBETXo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After deploying checkout-api v2.3.1 to production, the service failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. We rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging, so we did not use it.) After the rollback, the service is healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident for it, INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc is newer, but it was only ever healthy in staging, so it didn't qualify.\n- **Rollback:** us-east, us-west and eu-west all moved from v2.3.1 to v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** It says what happened, why I picked v2.3.0, and the results after the rollback. It also says the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure still needs to be found before v2.3.1 is redeployed.", "type": "text"}]}]}